<section class="integration-hero" aria-labelledby="integration-title">
  <div><span class="eyebrow">EXTERNAL AGENT INTEGRATION CENTER</span><h1 id="integration-title">Agent Integrations</h1><p class="integration-subtitle">Your agent. Our sales workflow.</p><p>Connect autonomous purchasing agents to your sales workflow. LeadCurrent allows authorized external AI agents to submit purchasing inquiries through a secure API. Submitted requests remain unverified until a human manager reviews them.</p>
    <div class="integration-actions"><a href="#examples" class="button">Start integrating <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><%= link_to "Download OpenAPI 3.1", agent_inquiries_openapi_path, class: "button secondary", data: { turbo: false } %></div>
    <p class="integration-caption">Any AI model. Ordinary HTTPS. No internal Copilot or Page Agent required.</p>
  </div>
  <aside class="integration-boundary" aria-label="Integration permissions"><span class="integration-dot" aria-hidden="true"></span><strong>One narrow permission</strong><code>inquiries:create</code><p>Your agent can open a conversation.<br>Your team decides what becomes a lead.</p><span class="integration-status">Identity remains unverified</span></aside>
</section>

<section class="integration-cards" aria-label="Connection overview">
  <article><span class="eyebrow">01 · CONNECTION</span><h2>One API endpoint</h2><p>POST a bounded JSON request to the workspace selected by your credential.</p></article>
  <article><span class="eyebrow">02 · AUTHENTICATION</span><h2>Workspace bearer token</h2><p>Manager-issued, revocable and scoped to inquiry submission.</p></article>
  <article><span class="eyebrow">03 · REQUEST FORMAT</span><h2>JSON in. Receipt out.</h2><p>Explicit fields, helpful errors and durable idempotency for safe retries.</p></article>
  <article><span class="eyebrow">04 · HUMAN CONTROL</span><h2>Review before CRM</h2><p>No automatic lead, purchase, completed contact or sales-stage change.</p></article>
</section>

<section class="integration-section" aria-labelledby="flow-title"><div class="integration-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">HOW IT CONNECTS</span><h2 id="flow-title">A clear path from request to relationship.</h2></div>
  <ol class="integration-flow"><% [["External AI Agent", "Configure any provider"], ["LeadCurrent API", "Authenticate + validate"], ["Agent Inquiries", "Unverified claims"], ["AI Qualification", "Optional manager action"], ["Human Approval", "Review + choose owner"], ["CRM Lead", "Existing business rules"]].each_with_index do |(title, detail), index| %><li><span><%= "%02d" % (index + 1) %></span><strong><%= title %></strong><small><%= detail %></small></li><% end %></ol>
</section>

<section class="integration-section integration-connection" id="connection" aria-labelledby="connection-title">
  <div><span class="eyebrow">CONNECTION DETAILS</span><h2 id="connection-title">A small contract.<br>A real integration.</h2><p>An outside company asks a LeadCurrent workspace manager for authorization. Your software only needs the endpoint, JSON schema, credential and permission to submit. It need not disclose its provider, prompts, private reasoning or system instructions.</p><p class="integration-caption">This page describes the current local implementation. Public Phase 3 deployment is pending approval; the existing Railway origin is not proof this API is deployed.</p></div>
  <div class="integration-surface"><dl class="integration-details"><div><dt>API base URL · this server</dt><dd><code><%= @guide.base_url %></code></dd></div><div><dt>Submission endpoint</dt><dd><code id="integration-endpoint"><%= @guide.endpoint %></code><button type="button" class="button small secondary" data-action="integration-copy#copy" data-copy-source="integration-endpoint" aria-label="Copy API endpoint">Copy endpoint</button></dd></div><div><dt>Method / format</dt><dd>POST · application/json request and response · 16 KB maximum body</dd></div><div><dt>Required headers</dt><dd><code>Authorization: Bearer YOUR_AGENT_TOKEN</code><code>Content-Type: application/json</code><code>Idempotency-Key: YOUR_UNIQUE_REQUEST_KEY</code></dd></div><div><dt>Retry safely</dt><dd>16–100 letters, digits or . _ : - per key. Same credential + key + payload returns the original receipt. Changed payload returns 409. Use a new key for a new inquiry.</dd></div></dl></div>
</section>

<section class="integration-section integration-auth" id="authentication" aria-labelledby="auth-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">AUTHENTICATION ≠ IDENTITY VERIFICATION</span><h2 id="auth-title">Authorized source.<br>Unverified business claims.</h2><p>A manager opens Manage Agent Credentials, names the integration and optionally sets an expiry. Copy the credential once and share it using a private approved channel. Store it in your client's environment, never source, URLs, prompts or logs. The server keeps only its digest.</p><p>The credential belongs to one workspace and can be revoked. It permits only <code>inquiries:create</code>. Browser cookies do not authenticate the API. Possession does not prove company identity, purchasing authority or an approved budget.</p></div><div class="integration-surface"><h3>Before you connect</h3><ul><li>Ask the destination workspace manager for access.</li><li>Keep the full token private; it cannot be recovered later.</li><li>Use HTTPS remotely; HTTP examples are loopback only.</li><li>Revoke a test or compromised credential promptly.</li></ul><%= link_to "Manage Agent Credentials →", agent_credentials_path, class: "button secondary" %><p class="integration-caption">Sign-in and manager role required. This public guide never displays a previously issued token.</p></div></section>

<section class="integration-section" id="examples" aria-labelledby="examples-title"><div class="integration-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">COPY. CONFIGURE. CONNECT.</span><h2 id="examples-title">Choose your tools.</h2><p>These examples create an <strong>actual fictional test inquiry</strong>. Configure <code>LEADCURRENT_AGENT_TOKEN</code> privately first; the placeholder is <code>YOUR_AGENT_TOKEN</code>. Examples use this server's origin. New runs generate new keys; keep the same key and unchanged body for an intentional retry. Do not use verbose HTTP logging.</p></div>
  <div class="integration-examples"><% [["curl", "cURL · Bash"], ["powershell", "PowerShell"], ["python", "Python · standard library"]].each do |key, label| %><details class="integration-code" <%= "open" if key == "curl" %>><summary><%= label %><span aria-hidden="true">+</span></summary><div class="integration-code-toolbar"><span>Creates a real test inquiry · no LLM calls</span><button type="button" class="button small secondary" data-action="integration-copy#copy" data-copy-source="example-<%= key %>" aria-label="Copy <%= label %> example">Copy example</button></div><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="<%= label %> request example"><code id="example-<%= key %>"><%= @guide.examples.fetch(key) %></code></pre></details><% end %></div>
  <p class="integration-copy-feedback" role="status" aria-live="polite" data-integration-copy-target="feedback"></p>
</section>

<section class="integration-section integration-connection" id="api-documentation" aria-labelledby="spec-title"><div><span class="eyebrow">MACHINE-READABLE DOCUMENTATION</span><h2 id="spec-title">One OpenAPI contract.<br>Bring your own agent.</h2><p>Download OpenAPI 3.1 and import the file or its URL into an OpenAPI-compatible client or agent framework. Select the local server or, after approved deployment, the existing HTTPS service. Configure the bearer credential privately in your own tool.</p><p>The contract describes the real POST route, fields, receipts, errors and idempotency header. It exposes no CRM records, credentials, model prompts or management endpoints. No MCP server or public agent registration is required.</p></div><div class="integration-surface"><h3>Developer resources</h3><%= link_to "Download OpenAPI specification", agent_inquiries_openapi_path, class: "button", data: { turbo: false } %><p><code><%= agent_inquiries_openapi_path %></code></p><a href="#authentication">Authentication guide →</a><a href="#testing">Testing instructions →</a><%= link_to "View Agent Inquiries →", agent_inquiries_path %></div></section>

<section class="integration-section" id="testing" aria-labelledby="testing-title"><div class="integration-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">TEST WITHOUT MODEL TOKENS</span><h2 id="testing-title">From your terminal to the inbox.</h2><p>Start the existing Rails/PostgreSQL application locally. Generate a manager-issued credential. In another terminal, set the base URL and enter the credential without placing its value in command history:</p></div>
  <div class="integration-surface"><pre tabindex="0" aria-label="Private PowerShell environment setup"><code>$env:LEADCURRENT_BASE_URL = '<%= @guide.base_url %>'
$credentialInput = Read-Host 'Agent credential (hidden)' -AsSecureString
$credentialPtr = [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::SecureStringToBSTR($credentialInput)
try {
  $env:LEADCURRENT_AGENT_TOKEN = [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::PtrToStringBSTR($credentialPtr)
} finally {
  [Runtime.InteropServices.Marshal]::ZeroFreeBSTR($credentialPtr)
}
python examples/purchasing_agent/client.py --mode deterministic</code></pre><p>The existing client generates a unique key, sends a real API request and prints its HTTP status and receipt. It consumes <strong>zero Groq tokens</strong>. Open Agent Inquiries to see pending_review / Identity: Unverified. An identical explicit key/body retry returns 200/replayed:true instead of creating another inquiry.</p><p>The included demo client has a fixed destination allowlist (local port 3100 and the existing production HTTPS origin; port 3170 is for the isolated verifier). If running Rails on another port, use the examples above. After deployment, set the base URL to <code>https://leadcurrent-production.up.railway.app</code>; verify health and the approved commit first, then use a short-lived test credential. No unrestricted browser CORS or tunnel is needed.</p></div>
  <div class="integration-test-grid"><article class="integration-surface"><h3>Optional real AI demonstration</h3><p>The existing Python client's <code>--mode ai</code> turns a purchasing goal into a real Groq-generated inquiry. It uses the same authenticated API and may consume free-tier tokens. It also needs private <code>GROQ_API_KEY</code> configuration. This is optional: other agents may use any model/provider, or no model at all.</p></article><article class="integration-surface"><h3>Human approval stays in control</h3><p>A manager may qualify the saved inquiry with AI, request information internally, reject it or accept it through the existing lead service. Missing contact details are never invented. On acceptance the normal 24-hour first-contact deadline begins; no purchase or completed contact is recorded.</p></article></div>
</section>

<section class="integration-section" aria-labelledby="errors-title"><div class="integration-section-heading"><span class="eyebrow">PREDICTABLE RESPONSES</span><h2 id="errors-title">Know what to do next.</h2></div><div class="integration-response-grid"><% [["201 / 200", "Created / safe replay", "Read inquiry_id, status, identity and replayed. A receipt is not a quotation or purchase."], ["400 / 422", "Check your request", "Use unique JSON fields, the documented types and lengths, and a valid idempotency header. No organization_id or status overrides."], ["401", "Check authorization", "Ask the workspace manager to check the token, scope, expiry or revocation. Do not send your credential in support screenshots."], ["409", "Conflicting retry", "Reuse the original body/key for a retry. Choose a new key only for an intentionally new inquiry."], ["413 / 415 / 405", "Check size and transport", "Use POST, application/json, no query parameters and a body no larger than 16,384 bytes."], ["429 / 503", "Wait before retrying", "Respect Retry-After: 60 on 429. Retry later with the same body/key; never bypass the workspace quota."]].each do |code, title, text| %><article class="integration-surface"><code><%= code %></code><h3><%= title %></h3><p><%= text %></p></article><% end %></div><p class="integration-caption">Limits are process-local: 60/IP, 10/credential, 30/workspace per minute. Multiple workers/replicas need a shared limiter. Inquiry status polling/editing and outbound clarification email are not provided. AI interpretation is fallible; business claims require human verification.</p></section>
